class Stack {
    int stack[];
    int top;
    int size;

    // Constructor
    Stack(int size) {
        this.size = size;
        stack = new int[size];
        top = -1;
    }

    // Push operation
    void push(int value) throws Exception {
        if (top == size - 1) {
            throw new Exception("Stack Overflow");
        }

        stack[++top] = value;
        System.out.println(value + " pushed into stack");
    }

    // Pop operation
    int pop() throws Exception {
        if (top == -1) {
            throw new Exception("Stack Underflow");
        }

        return stack[top--];
    }

    // Display operation
    void display() throws Exception {
        if (top == -1) {
            throw new Exception("Stack is Empty");
        }

        System.out.println("Stack elements:");

        for (int i = top; i >= 0; i--) {
            System.out.println(stack[i]);
        }
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Stack s = new Stack(3);

        try {
            s.push(10);
            s.push(20);
            s.push(30);

            s.display();

            System.out.println("Popped element: " + s.pop());
            System.out.println("Popped element: " + s.pop());

            s.display();

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.out.println("Exception: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}

Output
10 pushed into stack
20 pushed into stack
30 pushed into stack
Stack elements:
30
20
10
Popped element: 30
Popped element: 20
Stack elements:
10

Important points
ADT Stack → implements push, pop, and display.
Stack Overflow → occurs when the stack is full.
Stack Underflow → occurs when trying to pop from an empty stack.
try-catch → handles the exceptions.
throw new Exception() → generates the exception when an invalid operation occurs.
